  "description": "On\u202f15\u202fAugust\u202f2023 at\u202f14:23:10\u202fUTC the system logged an email\u2011opened event with the identifier\u202f5f8d0c5e-9b3a-4d2e-8f1c-2a7b6c9e3d1f. The recipient\u2019s IP address was\u202f203.0.113.42, originating from San\u202fFrancisco,\u202fCA, United\u202fStates (postal\u202f94103, latitude\u202f37.7749, longitude\u202f\u2011122.4194, timezone\u202fAmerica/Los_Angeles). The message itself (ID\u202fmsg_1234567890abcdef, version\u202f1.0) was sent by\u202fsender@example.org to\u202frecipient@example.com with the subject \u201cYour Weekly Update\u201d. It carried the tags \u201cnewsletter\u201d and \u201cweekly\u201d, used no template, and its internal timestamp was\u202f2023\u201108\u201115T14:22:45Z.  \n\nThe email was opened at\u202f2023\u201108\u201115T14:22:45Z from the same IP (203.0.113.42); the location field was null, and the user\u2011agent string recorded was \u201cMozilla/5.0 (Windows NT\u202f10.0;\u202fWin64;\u202fx64) AppleWebKit/537.36\u201d. Parsing that user agent confirmed a non\u2011mobile Windows\u202f10 desktop (OS company Microsoft,\u202fhttps://www.microsoft.com; OS family Windows; OS icon \u201cwindows\u201d; OS URL\u202fhttps://www.microsoft.com/windows) running Google Chrome\u202f115.0.0.0 (browser type \u201cbrowser\u201d, UA company Google,\u202fhttps://www.google.com, UA icon \u201cchrome\u201d, UA URL\u202fhttps://www.google.com/chrome/). A click followed a few seconds later at\u202f2023\u201108\u201115T14:23:10Z, also from\u202f203.0.113.42 (location \u201cSan\u202fFrancisco,\u202fCA,\u202fUS\u201d), using the same Windows\u202f10 Chrome user\u2011agent and directing the user to\u202fhttps://example.com/landing-page. The SMTP log shows the message was sent at\u202f2023\u201108\u201115T14:22:30Z, size\u202f10\u202f240\u202fbytes, from source IP\u202f203.0.113.42 to destination IP\u202f198.51.100.25 with a \u201c250\u202fOK\u201d diagnostic response. Metadata attached to the message includes the user ID\u202f987\u202f654, and no resends were recorded."
